  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`TimeAsserter.ExecuteAsync` no longer blocks a thread for as long as it runs.** It took the machine-wide performance-test lock, a system mutex, on a `Task.Run` thread, as only the thread that takes a mutex may release it, and waited there synchronously for the scenario, which stalled while the thread pool was busy. The turn is now Compze.Threading.Interprocess's `IProcessLock`, a file in `Compze` in the temp directory, which `ExecuteAsync` awaits and holds across the scenario's awaits. A performance test waits up to five minutes for its turn instead of two, and one that gives up says which performance test, in which process, holds it. The processes that share a temp directory share the turn: on Windows that makes it per user, where the mutex was per machine.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.Internals.SystemCE 0.12.0-internal (was 0.10.0-internal), Compze.Threading 0.14.0-alpha (was 0.13.0-alpha), Compze.Threading.Interprocess 0.8.0-alpha (was 0.7.1-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
